      "@type": "FAQPage",
      "@id": "https://www.stselectronicrecyclinginc.com/bakersfield-ca#faqpage",
      "mainEntity": [
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "What certifications and standards guide your work?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "STS supports documented recycling and data-handling workflows using recognized standards and customer records. Depending on the project, documentation may reference NIST 800-88, HIPAA safeguards, ISO 27001 controls, SOC 2 requirements, or DoD 5220.22-M procedures. The applicable workflow depends on the equipment, data sensitivity, customer policy, and requested reporting."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "What areas do you serve?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "STS coordinates electronics recycling for Bakersfield, Kern County, and organizations across the broader San Joaquin Valley and Central Valley. Service planning considers equipment volume, pickup access, business schedules, and whether the project includes computers, displays, servers, networking equipment, or data-bearing media. Organizations searching for electronics recycling near me in Bakersfield can request scheduled pickup across Kern County."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "How long does pickup take?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "Scheduling depends on project scope, equipment volume, access conditions, and route availability. Many business requests can be reviewed promptly, and same-week scheduling may be available. Send an inventory summary to receive a practical timing estimate. STS engagements with agricultural, energy, and institutional operations typically account for loading access, production schedules, and equipment separation before transportation."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "Do you provide audit documentation?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "STS can provide project records such as equipment inventories, pickup documentation, data disposition records, certificates of destruction, and downstream reporting when applicable. Documentation is organized around the agreed scope and the customer's internal retention requirements. Corporate IT managers typically expect serial-level records and a clear chain of custody when assets move through multiple departments."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "What happens to equipment after pickup?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "Equipment is received, sorted, and directed to the appropriate reuse, recovery, data-handling, or material-processing workflow. Data-bearing equipment is handled according to the selected disposition method, while recyclable materials are separated for responsible downstream recovery. The final record can identify the equipment category, selected disposition, and documentation available for the project."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "Is pickup free?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "Pickup is available at no cost for qualifying volumes and project conditions. Transportation details depend on equipment mix, location, access, and requested services. STS reviews those factors before confirming the pickup plan and applicable project terms. A project estimate can account for quantity, loading conditions, data services, and reporting requirements before scheduling."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "What electronics can be recycled in Bakersfield?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "Bakersfield organizations can recycle computers, laptops, cell phones, networking equipment, servers, printers, copiers, ink and toner, monitors, and older electronics through a coordinated program. STS can combine asset records, data handling, transportation, reuse evaluation, and material recovery based on the equipment mix and project requirements."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "How does the electronics recycling process work?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "The process begins with an equipment list, estimated volume, access details, and preferred timing. STS reviews transportation, data-bearing assets, and reporting needs before pickup. Equipment is then collected, documented, and routed through the appropriate workflow, while reusable and recyclable materials move through separate recovery paths."
          }
        }
      ]
